{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSC4aK2qWqsY2bX6mEHq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I split the system prompt into two cached blocks, so a `save_fact` now invalidates only the per-athlete block. The fix is in place and passes a fake-LLM check, but I couldn't confirm it against the live API. The static block may also be too small for Anthropic to cache at all.\n\n**The change** (`bot.py`, `build_system()`): the static `INSTRUCTIONS` block and the athlete context (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language) are now separate text blocks, each with an ephemeral `cache_control` marker. Nothing else changed. ANSWER.md has the details; nothing is committed.\n\n**What I checked:** a scratch script outside the repo runs `reply()` with a fake LLM. It saves a fact, then sends another message. The static block is byte-identical across rounds, athletes and dates, the fact appears only in the athlete block, and the tools list is unchanged. All assertions pass. I couldn't check real cache behaviour because there's no `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY` and the `anthropic` SDK isn't installed here.\n\n**Open risk:** Sonnet won't cache a prefix under 1024 tokens. The cached prefix at the static block is the tools array plus the instructions, and the log suggests that's roughly 1,000 tokens, right at the line. If it's under, the split does nothing. After deploying, check the message following a `save_fact`: `cache_read_input_tokens` should be close to the static size, and `cache_creation_input_tokens` should be only the athlete tail. If creation is near the full prompt, the fix is to lengthen the static instructions. I didn't pad them with filler, since that changes what the bot is told.\n\n**Not fixed:** keyword-triggered tool groups (`plan_week`, `predict_race`) still evict everything, since tools sit above the system prompt. The log shows creation of about 1,300 tokens on those calls. Fixing it means dropping the tool filtering, which NOTES.md credits with about 75% fewer tool tokens, so I left it as your call.\n\n**Colleague's note:** I applied the two-marker split, the rule that the static block contains no interpolated values, and the tools-above-system warning. The top-N fact selection and the 55-tool story don't apply to this bot, and the 780-token figure doesn't transfer, because this bot's static prefix sits close to the minimum."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":235,"cache_read_input_tokens":46096,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":235},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41269cc4-3c06-4032-a991-53c3648c9774","uuid":"f97ff1ff-7285-45b9-a65f-697852c37c1f","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:29:51.676Z","request_id":"req_011CgSC4a4eCNid6NgYWnXRv"}
